WEBVTT

00:24:27.079 --> 00:24:32.704
And I was such a fan of that show and
the specificity of it that it felt.

00:24:33.663 --> 00:24:36.371
For me, I remember when I first
saw it, I thought, oh, no,

00:24:37.121 --> 00:24:39.579
like it didn't matter how good everyone
was because they were great.

00:24:39.621 --> 00:24:43.329
It felt like it was somehow sacrilege
that it was redoing exactly

00:24:43.329 --> 00:24:46.871
the same thing in essentially the
same time period, you know,

00:24:46.871 --> 00:24:49.038
putting it through the American TV mill.

00:24:49.038 --> 00:24:51.371
And then you realize, oh, they're
doing it perfectly.

00:24:51.371 --> 00:24:54.871
And it's it's exactly what it should be.
And it's its own thing.

00:24:54.996 --> 00:24:58.038
It was the quality of the show
that that won me over.

00:24:58.329 --> 00:25:03.663
OK, next question. I'm sure you hate
getting asked about Star Wars in